00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.500
FRANCESC CAMPOY: They're
very good, especially--

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.890
so basically the
preemptible machine,

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.630
a preemptible VM is a VM that
can be preempted, obviously,

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:08.024
and has a limit that it
cannot run more than 24 hours.

00:02:08.024 --> 00:02:10.919
So regardless of what
happens after 24 hours,

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:12.190
it will be shut down.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.800
But it could be shut
down faster than that.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.580
But you have the power
to react to that.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.480
There is actually
an API call that

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.090
is done before it's shut down.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.950
So you can shut down gracefully
if you need to release

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.180
some resources or whatever.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.660
You can toy with that.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.690
