00:06:34.034 --> 00:06:35.450
Why don't you tell
us a little bit

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.510
about-- so yeah, if
I was a PHP developer

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.320
and I get to go Google
Cloud Platform, what

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:42.594
do we have at my disposal?

00:06:42.594 --> 00:06:44.260
TERRY RYAN: Well, we
have the wide range

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.980
of all of Google Cloud Platform,
but specifically focused

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:51.220
on computing resources, it would
be App Engine, Compute Engine,

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.040
and Container Engine.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.990
For App Engine, PHP is one of
those standard languages that

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:58.970
runs on App Engine standard,
which means that you can take

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:01.960
PHP code that you use in
other places, plop it down,

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.670
and it will run right within
the context of App Engine

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:05.745
relatively easily.

00:07:05.745 --> 00:07:07.370
Of all the languages
that imported code

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:11.380
over from non-App
Engine to App Engine,

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.260
I feel like the PHP implantation
is the lightest in terms

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.420
of what you have to change.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.960
You have to change a couple
places where you point

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.500
to the file system, because
on App Engine, you can't.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.230
But you get rid of those
calls and for the most part,

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.520
a lot of your PHP code
is just going to work,

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.027
it's really kind of fantastic.

00:07:28.027 --> 00:07:29.860
So we've got App Engine
standard and we also

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.070
have App Engine
flexible runtime,

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.120
PHP is supported
on both of those,

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.750
in addition to Compute
Engine and Container Engine.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:37.666
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:42.700
So for PHP standard
environment in App Engine,

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:44.141
can you use any
kind of framework?

00:07:44.141 --> 00:07:45.640
Like you were talking
